# Project Folder Structure

All work lives under `src/`. Never dump logic into random files.

```
src/
  App.tsx              # Routes ONLY live here (react-router)
  main.tsx             # App bootstrap
  components/          # Reusable UI (no feature business logic)
    ui/                # shadcn/ui primitives (add via CLI, then customize)
    common/            # Shared composites: Header, EmptyState, etc.
  pages/               # One folder per route/page (composers only)
  features/            # Domain modules (auth, dashboard, etc.)
    <feature>/
      components/      # Feature-specific components
      hooks/           # Feature-specific hooks
      types.ts
      index.ts         # Public exports only
  hooks/               # Shared custom hooks
  stores/              # Zustand stores (create only when needed)
  services/            # API / external data layer
  types/               # Shared TypeScript types
  utils/               # Pure helpers (no React)
  lib/                 # Shared libs (e.g. shadcn `cn` helper)
  constants/           # App-wide constants
  assets/              # Images, fonts, static media
  styles/              # Global / shared styles (includes Tailwind + shadcn theme)
```

## Rules

- Small change → still place it in the correct folder. No one-off files at `src/` root.
- Big feature → create `features/<name>/` with its own `components/`, `hooks/`, `types.ts`.
- Pages compose reusable components + features; they do not own low-level UI markup.
- If a required folder is missing, create it before writing code.
- Prefer `index.ts` barrels for clean public exports from features/components.
---

# Guidance

If the user asks to put code in the wrong place (e.g. page UI inside `App.tsx`, API calls in a Button, store in a page file), **stop and explain** the correct folder and why before implementing.
